id "8c8f3e39-d3c1-5e7f-a209-959cacdc0344" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396525} {:answer/id #uuid "b60dd011-c5bd-5d35-bf92-6b2b7e46ffc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c8f3e39-d3c1-5e7f-a209-959cacdc0344" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396525} :answer-field/id #uuid "309e3e22-428f-58e4-8c8d-2ab6315d5bb2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e1bc76f0-5438-50ce-a2c1-3d7bf5ef80b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-334924" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"170px\">$3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"170px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95223ee8-46d8-58c2-9e3b-017adb2789e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution of an Inhomogeneous System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "508628f6-63a5-5e6a-a776-4ba0722db871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "508628f6-63a5-5e6a-a776-4ba0722db871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479476} :answer-field/id #uuid "1954211e-be5b-5ec7-9793-f1e117c5135a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d30f021-ca55-5b32-8ba2-aebcfc919c9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d30f021-ca55-5b32-8ba2-aebcfc919c9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479426} :answer-field/id #uuid "b68e6796-375b-5d49-8e2e-66926ee5d502" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55496bb1-52a1-5f42-8a88-3b3b54310c44" :question/math-academy-id "q-334927" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"100px\">$5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-1))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"100px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308724 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8e79b01-2389-5a91-bd1b-47d545c124e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307021} {:answer/id #uuid "06fe7ba9-e60a-5a45-b758-fa0196ee521e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06fe7ba9-e60a-5a45-b758-fa0196ee521e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479370} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1add94-bde4-538a-ae6f-d06b8a3019c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19468931-2ce6-5bd0-af7b-5212e5297c87" :question/math-academy-id "q-335085" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b710ba-ff00-564b-aa56-a218823c5a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370308} {:answer/id #uuid "115a425c-7d5a-5e6a-a6a9-f0d774f944ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370309} {:answer/id #uuid "039d6594-16e9-5ee1-a93f-756747ec02c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370310} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c3a851-f331-52ed-aa7f-b2a15aaca90c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "039d6594-16e9-5ee1-a93f-756747ec02c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370310} :answer-field/id #uuid "04307a93-eb46-548d-9a4a-4bf90a0e6697" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9fcadd6-0c1a-598a-b135-72da1abeb4f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-335088" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3x(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s))\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308736 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f2cc77d-908e-5975-babf-c7e95d32af6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306066} {:answer/id #uuid "6d657aec-32ba-5cf6-9bf5-c39f0c00dc78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306197} {:answer/id #uuid "851c1af3-2a69-5a9e-aeb2-bdc919879a73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306419} {:answer/id #uuid "b970e691-2738-5a66-b02c-0fc82876b459" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f2cc77d-908e-5975-babf-c7e95d32af6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306066} :answer-field/id #uuid "99185d97-eb59-509d-8409-76c2030ce0cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d6b9f30-3747-520a-a2bd-7bc874e4c993" :question/math-academy-id "q-335127" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"100px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "556a1d6d-0b97-5b9c-919a-ffcaef348e99" :answer/type {:db/id #ed